module

public import Theory.Representation.Mathieu.SmallModules.M12DegreeGap.PointSimpleDegrees.Data

/-!
# Candidate coordinates for the native M₁₁ eleven-coset flag

The words represent left cosets g⟨AB⟩. `leftAction` lists proposed images
under left multiplication by A and B. The packed basis columns express
adapted vectors in the coset ordering. The inverse columns go in the reverse
direction; the adapted action columns should equal P⁻¹ A P and P⁻¹ B P.

All identities still require kernel-checked certificates. In particular this
module does not assert a coset enumeration, an invertible basis, or a flag.
The canonical diagonal blocks are the independent `Data.modelMatrix` values.
See `source/README.md`; source context: James, J. Algebra 27 (1973), 57–111.
-/

